-- Local dummy data: preserves all 163 original ticket rows and dates.
-- Apply db/2026-10-09-ticket-pricing.sql first for an existing database.
-- Referenced events must exist, and ticket IDs 1..163 must be unused.
-- The ticket_price_history table from backup.sql must already exist.
-- Initial price equals current price; the dummy floor is 60% of that price.
-- Only future, unsold-out tickets enable automatic pricing.
-- Observation starts 121 minutes ago, so enabled tickets are due on the next scan.
-- sold_ticket is cumulative dummy inventory; it does not create PAID orders.
-- With no recent PAID orders, enabled tickets will discount on the next scan.
USE free_ticket;
SET NAMES utf8mb4;
SET time_zone = '+09:00';
SET @ticket_seed_now = NOW(6);
SET @ticket_seed_observed_from = DATE_SUB(@ticket_seed_now, INTERVAL 121 MINUTE);

START TRANSACTION;

